#Concatenating Lists

'''
We can concatenate two lists together 
with the addition operator (+).
'''
states2 = ['Arizona', 'Ohio', 'Louisiana']

'''
Then declare a new variable named best_states, and 
assign to it the value of concatenating the states 
and states2 lists together:
'''
best_states = states = states2

print(best_states)

#slicing lists
'''
To slice a list means to retrieve a subsection of it,
This does not alter the original list. 
To slice a list, we use bracket notation along with a colon.
'''
# retrieves list items from best_states with index 1-3, 
#not including 3 (so, index 1 and 2)
print(best_states[1:3])

# retrieves list items starting from the beginning, to
#index 2, but not including 2 (so, index 0 and 1). 
print(best_states[:2])

# retrieves list items starting from index 4, 
#all the way to the end.
print(best_states[4:])








